{"availability":"available","full":"chriskhanhtran/bert-extractive-summarization","name":"bert-extractive-summarization","description":"MobileBERT and DistilBERT for extractive summarization","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":94,"forks":29,"created":"2020-05-23T17:28:46Z","updated":"2023-06-12T21:27:02Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://extractive-summarization.herokuapp.com/","topics":[],"demo":"https://extractive-summarization.herokuapp.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.616Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.616Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.616Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.616Z","stars":94,"forks":29}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["In an effort to make BERTSUM (Liu et al., 2019) lighter and faster for low-resource devices, I fine-tuned DistilBERT (Sanh et al., 2019) and MobileBERT (Sun et al., 2019), two lite versions of BERT on CNN/DailyMail dataset. DistilBERT has the same performance as BERT-base while being 45% smaller. MobileBERT is 4x smaller and 2.7x faster than BERT-base yet retains 94% of its performance.","I modified the source codes in PreSumm to use the HuggingFace's transformers library and their pretrained DistilBERT model. At the moment (05/31/2020), MobileBERT is not yet available in transformers. Fortunately, I found this PyTorch implementation of MobileBERT by @lonePatient.","Please visit PreSumm for instructions for training on CNN/DailyMail and this modified repo forked from PreSumm for fine-tuning DistilBERT and MobileBERT."],"features":["Demo with MobileBert: Open"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chriskhanhtran/bert-extractive-summarization/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"d55c7d935b61dda919a9592e8d3afac2b7b5f5bea53fff6c8d042f226bfe3a6e","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.737Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:59:12.737Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"In an effort to make BE